# La Mafia Game - Cursor Rules

## Project Patterns

### Code Organization

- Use Astro for page routing and layouts
- Vue components for interactive elements
- Keep components small and focused
- Follow atomic design principles

### Naming Conventions

- Components: PascalCase (e.g., GameRoom.vue)
- Files: kebab-case (e.g., game-room.astro)
- Functions: camelCase (e.g., createGameRoom)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., GAME_PHASES)

### File Structure

- Pages in src/pages/
- Components in src/components/
- Layouts in src/layouts/
- Types in src/types/
- Utils in src/utils/

### Component Patterns

- Use Composition API
- Keep state management simple
- Prefer props over events
- Document component props

### State Management

- Local state for component-specific data
- Supabase for shared state
- Real-time subscriptions for game state
- Avoid complex state management libraries

## Development Preferences

### Code Style

- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Follow ESLint rules
- Use Prettier for formatting
- Write meaningful comments

### Testing

- Unit tests for utilities
- Component tests for UI
- Integration tests for game flow
- E2E tests for critical paths
- Use vitest as testing engine and vue test utils to test vue3 components

### Documentation

- Keep README up to date
- Document API endpoints
- Comment complex logic
- Update memory bank regularly

### Git Workflow

- Feature branches
- Semantic versioning
- Conventional commits
- Pull request reviews

## Project Intelligence

### Critical Paths

1. Authentication Flow

   - Login/Register
   - Session management
   - Profile updates

2. Game Flow

   - Room creation
   - Player joining
   - Role assignment
   - Game phases
   - Voting system

3. Real-time Updates
   - Game state changes
   - Player status
   - Chat messages
   - Voting results

### Known Challenges

1. Real-time Synchronization

   - Handle disconnections
   - Manage state conflicts
   - Ensure consistency

2. Game State Management

   - Complex state transitions
   - Role-based permissions
   - Action validation

3. User Experience
   - Mobile responsiveness
   - Performance optimization
   - Accessibility

### Tool Usage

- VS Code for development
- Chrome DevTools for debugging
- Postman for API testing
- Vercel for deployment

## Evolution Tracking

### Technical Decisions

- Astro for static generation
- Vue.js for interactivity
- Supabase for backend
- TailwindCSS for styling

### Architecture Changes

- Initial: Basic Astro setup
- Current: Adding Vue components
- Planned: Supabase integration

### Performance Considerations

- Lazy loading components
- Optimizing images
- Minimizing bundle size
- Caching strategies
